    debrief: 'Total disputed exposure is $5,689.99 across six transactions. The $3,500 from txn 31 (QuickTransfer) represents 61.5% of total exposure. SUM(amount) on a filtered dataset is a one-liner — but the next question is always how much of that has been resolved vs. is still open. Two follow-on approaches: Approach A — join transactions to disputes on txn_id, then filter resolved_at IS NOT NULL to get resolved exposure vs. IS NULL for unresolved. Approach B — use conditional aggregation in one query: SUM(CASE WHEN d.resolved_at IS NULL THEN t.amount ELSE 0 END) AS unresolved_exposure, SUM(CASE WHEN d.resolved_at IS NOT NULL THEN t.amount ELSE 0 END) AS resolved_exposure. Approach B returns a single row with both numbers — the analyst deliverable format. The distinction between gross disputed (all disputed txns) and net disputed (still open) is the core compliance question: one number is for reporting, the other is for action.',
