    hints: ['What does one row in your result represent? Your output needs 2 rows with columns: account_id, company_name, total_users, never_active, inactive_pct.', 'CASE WHEN ... THEN ... ELSE ... END works like if-else inside SQL. You can use it inside aggregate functions for conditional counts.'],
